// Longer stories for major myths and legends
window.STORY={
"Gilgamesh of Uruk":["Gilgamesh, two-thirds god, oppresses his city, so the gods create the wild man Enkidu as his match. They become friends, slay the forest guardian Humbaba and the Bull of Heaven, and the gods punish them by killing Enkidu.","Terrified of death, Gilgamesh travels to Utnapishtim, survivor of the flood, who tells him the story of the deluge. Gilgamesh finds a plant of youth, but a snake steals it while he bathes. He returns to Uruk and accepts that his walls and his name are his immortality."],
"Osiris, Isis & Horus":["Osiris, king of Egypt, is murdered by his jealous brother Set, who cuts his body into pieces and scatters them along the Nile. His wife Isis searches the land, gathers the pieces, and with magic brings him back long enough to conceive a son.","Osiris becomes lord of the dead. Their son Horus grows up to fight Set for the throne, losing an eye in the struggle. Every pharaoh ruled as the living Horus and became Osiris in death."],
"Fall of Troy":["Paris, prince of Troy, carries off Helen, wife of King Menelaus of Sparta. The Greeks sail with a thousand ships and besiege Troy for ten years. Achilles kills Hector and is killed in turn by an arrow to his heel.","Finally the Greeks build a hollow wooden horse, hide warriors inside, and pretend to sail away. The Trojans drag it into the city, and that night the Greeks open the gates. Archaeologists have found a real city at Hisarlik, Turkey, destroyed around this time."],
"Romulus & Remus found Rome":["Twin sons of the war god Mars and a Vestal priestess are thrown into the Tiber by a jealous king. A she-wolf suckles them and a shepherd raises them.","Grown, they decide to found a city but quarrel over where. Romulus builds a wall on the Palatine Hill; when Remus mockingly jumps over it, Romulus kills him and names the city Rome. Romans counted their years from this date."],
"Prometheus & Pandora":["The Titan Prometheus tricks Zeus at a sacrifice and then steals fire from the gods for humankind. Zeus chains him to a rock in the Caucasus, where an eagle eats his liver every day; Heracles eventually frees him.","As punishment for humans, Zeus has the first woman, Pandora, made and given a jar. She opens it and releases sickness, toil and all evils into the world. Only hope remains inside."],
"Prose Edda":["The world begins in the gap between fire and ice. Odin and his brothers kill the frost giant Ymir and build the world from his body. The world tree Yggdrasil links nine realms, including Asgard, home of the gods, and Midgard, home of humans.","At Ragnarök, the wolf Fenrir swallows Odin, Thor and the World Serpent kill each other, and fire consumes the world. Then a new green earth rises from the sea and two humans begin again."],
"Mahabharata":["Two branches of a royal family, the five Pandava brothers and their hundred Kaurava cousins, fight over the kingdom of Hastinapura. The Pandavas lose everything in a rigged game of dice and are exiled for thirteen years.","At the great battle of Kurukshetra, the archer Arjuna hesitates to kill his own relatives. His charioteer, the god Krishna, teaches him about duty and the soul in the Bhagavad Gita. The Pandavas win, but at terrible cost."],
"Ramayana":["Prince Rama of Ayodhya is exiled to the forest with his wife Sita and brother Lakshmana. The demon king Ravana kidnaps Sita and carries her to Lanka.","With the monkey god Hanuman and an army of monkeys and bears, Rama builds a bridge to Lanka, kills Ravana and rescues Sita. The festival of Diwali celebrates his return home."],
"Kojiki":["The gods Izanagi and Izanami stir the ocean with a jewelled spear, and the drops form the islands of Japan. Izanami dies giving birth to fire, and Izanagi follows her to the land of the dead but flees in horror.","From his washing are born the sun goddess Amaterasu and the storm god Susanoo. When Susanoo's rampages make Amaterasu hide in a cave, the world goes dark until the gods lure her out with a mirror and laughter. Japan's emperors traditionally trace their line to her."],
"Journey to the West":["Sun Wukong, a monkey born from a stone, learns magic, wreaks havoc in heaven, and is trapped under a mountain by the Buddha for 500 years.","He is freed to protect the monk Xuanzang on a pilgrimage to India to fetch Buddhist scriptures, together with the pig-man Zhu Bajie and the river ogre Sha Wujing. The journey is loosely based on a real monk's trip in 629 to 645."],
"Popol Vuh":["The gods try to make people from mud and from wood, but both fail. In between, the Hero Twins Hunahpu and Xbalanque are summoned to Xibalba, the underworld, to play the ball game against the lords of death.","They survive the houses of darkness, knives, cold and jaguars, let themselves be killed, return to life, and trick the lords into their own deaths. They rise as the sun and moon, and humans are finally made from maize."],
"Epic of Sundiata":["Sundiata Keita is born unable to walk and mocked as a child. One day he pulls himself up on an iron rod and walks, and he grows into a great hunter.","Exiled with his mother, he returns to lead the Mandinka against the sorcerer-king Sumanguru, whose power is broken by a cockspur arrow. Sundiata founds the Mali Empire. Griots still perform the epic today."],
"Dangun founds Gojoseon":["Hwanung, son of the lord of heaven, descends to Mount Taebaek. A bear and a tiger ask to become human; he tells them to stay in a cave and eat only mugwort and garlic for 100 days.","The tiger gives up, but the bear becomes a woman. She marries Hwanung and bears Dangun, who founds Gojoseon, the first Korean kingdom. South Korea marks it on National Foundation Day, 3 October."],
"Ilya Muromets":["The son of peasants, Ilya cannot walk for 33 years until wandering pilgrims heal him and give him great strength.","He rides to Kyiv to serve Prince Vladimir, defeating the monstrous Nightingale the Robber, whose whistle flattens forests, and defending Rus' against invaders."],
"Kitezh, the invisible city":["When Batu Khan's Mongol army approached, the people of Greater Kitezh prayed rather than fought. The city sank beneath the waters of Lake Svetloyar, or vanished into the mist.","Pilgrims say that on quiet summer nights you can still hear the church bells under the lake, and only the pure of heart can find the way to the city."]
};
